Local Optimize on Debian/Ubuntu
================================

The Ubuntu 26.04/amd64 package installs application code, a relocatable
Python 3.14 Intel XPU environment, pinned E5/Qwen models and the pinned
qwen2.5-coder:7b manifest/blobs. Installation does not run pip or download
models. Runtime files are installed on the root filesystem under
/usr/lib/local-optimize and /usr/share/ollama; use an SSD for that filesystem.

Prerequisites are an Intel GPU driver/OpenCL ICD, PostgreSQL 18 with pgvector,
and an installed Ollama binary/service with the ollama system user and the
standard /usr/share/ollama/.ollama/models store. PostgreSQL and pgvector are
package dependencies. Ollama is checked by preinst because this host installs
it outside dpkg.

Configure ~/.config/local-optimize/secrets.env and projects.json as described
in /usr/share/doc/local-optimize/docs/installation.md. Package installation
cannot safely invent database credentials or bearer tokens. Keep real secrets
out of the repository.

Commands:

  local-optimize migrate        Apply PostgreSQL migrations
  local-optimize server         Run the FastAPI server
  local-optimize watchdog       Run filesystem indexing
  local-optimize mcp            Run the full local-only MCP server
  local-optimize lmstudio-mcp   Run the read-only LM Studio wrapper
  local-optimize index          Index the registered project

LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_VENV can override /usr/lib/local-optimize/venv for development.
LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_ROOT can override /usr/lib/local-optimize for packaging checks.

The user units are installed but not globally enabled. After configuration,
apply migrations and check the server, then enable them for the intended user:

  local-optimize migrate
  systemctl --user enable --now gpu-rag-server.service watchdog-indexer.service

Verify /liveness, /readiness and /runtime before registering local-only agents.
Cloud-capable clients must not receive direct RAG MCP access. Existing allowed
agent entries should use /usr/bin/local-optimize mcp (or lmstudio-mcp for the
isolated LM Studio wrapper).
